SUMMARY:90 Minutes of Innovation: Networks\, Intelligence & the Future of D
 ecision-Making 
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 6 spots left
 \nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/e
 vents/180910\n\n1:00PM Program\, 2:30PM Networking\nWhat can we learn from
  the individuals shaping AI\, enterprise transformation\, and modern engin
 eering at the highest levels?\n\nIn the latest edition of 90 Minutes of In
 novation\, John Werner - venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI
  columnist - will lead a series of one-on-one conversations with three rem
 arkable leaders\, each offering a distinct perspective on innovation\, lea
 dership\, and the moment we’re in.\n\nJon Hirschtick\, founder of SolidW
 orks and Onshape\, is a pioneering force in computer-aided design who has 
 transformed how engineers and designers build the world. An MIT alumnus\, 
 he used winnings from the Institute’s legendary blackjack team to launch
  his first company - an experience that later inspired the film 21.\n\nSan
 dy Pentland\, MIT professor with appointments at MIT and Stanford\, and on
 e of the most cited data scientists globally\, whose work on human behavio
 r\, social networks\, and “reality mining” has fundamentally reshaped 
 how we understand trust\, cities\, and collective intelligence. He will sp
 eak on his recent book\, Shared Wisdom: Cultural Evolution in the Age of 
 AI.\n\nDavid Kenny\, Executive Chairman of Nielsen and former CEO of IBM W
 atson\, with prior leadership roles at Akamai and The Weather Channel\, ha
 s operated at the forefront of AI\, data\, and global enterprise transform
 ation.\n\nThrough individual interviews\, the afternoon will explore their
  personal journeys\, the ideas that have defined their work\, and how each
  sees the rapidly evolving landscape of AI\, technology\, and innovation t
 oday. Expect an engaging\, insight-rich experience that connects lived exp
 erience with forward-looking perspective - offering a rare window into how
  these leaders think\, build\, and lead.\n\n*This event is complimentary a
 nd reserved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180910
